        <div id="edge-support" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Why Does Edge Support Matter for Getting In and Out of Bed?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Edge support is the most overlooked spec for seniors. Most people get up by sitting on the edge and pushing to stand. If the edge sags, you sit lower and tilted toward the floor, and standing gets harder.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What a strong edge is made of</h3>

          <p>
            Good edges come from the coil unit: thicker perimeter coils, a foam rail, or both. Helix describes reinforced perimeter coils on the Midnight Luxe, Leesa reinforced side coils, and Purple edge support foam it says makes getting in and out easier.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why all-foam beds usually lose</h3>

          <p>
            An all-foam mattress has nothing stiff at the perimeter, so the edge compresses like the middle. That is the main reason the TEMPUR-Cloud ranks last despite its pressure relief.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Usable sleep surface</h3>

          <p>
            On a weak edge, sleepers drift toward the middle. That matters for couples on a queen and for anyone who sleeps near the edge to reach a cane or a nightstand.
          </p>

          <p>
            Heavier sleepers stress edges most; see our guide to mattresses for heavy people. During the trial, sit on the edge for a minute and check whether your hips end up lower than your knees.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="height" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. How Tall Should a Mattress Be for Seniors?
          </h2>

          <p>
            What matters is total sitting height: frame plus foundation plus mattress. A common guideline is that your feet rest flat on the floor with knees at roughly a right angle when you sit on the edge.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">A practical way to measure</h3>

          <p>
            Measure from the floor to the seat of a firm chair you stand up from easily. That is a good target for the mattress edge. Your leg length decides, not a chart.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
